    "source_crystallography": "The compound2 CIF is retained privately as provenance. Its asymmetric unit contains separate symmetry-related molecular portions; the public graph records one complete molecule, with the N3–N1(sym)–N2(sym)–N2–N1–N3(sym) chain and B coordination to the corresponding terminal/central N pair. Do not merge crystallographically independent B1/B2 portions into one molecule.",
    "shared_geometry": "Optimize complete2 without deleting triflates; transfer the mapped B2N6 plus terminal N-CH2 anchor coordinates to1/3/4, freeze that common core and relax substituents only. The common geometry is generated by the solver, not supplied as an answer. Retain relaxed calculations for all four as the other comparison.",
